y numbers are what they were actually paid when they got placed. Tap any short to watch. ShortsFresher to 5.5 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Adarsh ]Adarsh V.SOC Analyst · UST Shorts3 → 4.8 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Hiba ]Hiba N.Security Analyst · IBS Shorts4 → 9.5 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Jithin ]Jithin R.Pentester · Consultancy ShortsFresher to 5 LPA[ Shorts thumbnail: Amala ]Amala K.SOC Analyst · GCC Want to talk to someone who has done it?Request an alumni call Why now Why cyber security, and why now. Every digitising business becomes a target, and India faces a documented shortage of security professionals. Defence is a skill learned by doing: reading logs, finding weaknesses and responding to incidents, which is exactly how this course is built. 750K+Unfilled security rolesIndia\'s cyber talent gap keeps demand ahead of supply year after year. 24/7SOCs never closeSecurity operations centres hire continuously across services and GCCs. ZeroLayoff-resistant fieldSecurity budgets survive downturns; breaches are costlier than salaries. Why it is a smart move for you Hands-on from week oneYou attack and defend lab machines, not memorise definitions. SOC-ready skillsSIEM, log analysis and incident playbooks: the exact work of your first job. Certification path built inStructured prep for CompTIA Security+, the baseline recruiters screen for. Cloud security includedAWS and identity security, because that is where companies actually run. Eligibility Is Cyber Security right for you? Security suits curious, methodical minds. IT and engineering backgrounds help, but motivated graduates from any stream succeed with the lab-first approach. A strong fit if you areA B.Tech, BCA or B.Sc graduate targeting security rolesAn IT support or network professional stepping upA developer or sysadmin adding security depthA fresher aiming for SOC analyst rolesA career switcher fascinated by how attacks work What you will needA graduate degree, IT exposure helpfulAround 9 hours a week for five monthsA laptop that can run virtual machinesNo hacking experience required [ counsellor photo ]Not sure you qualify?A counsellor reviews your background and tells you honestly. Free, no pressure.Check my eligibility → The full course Curriculum, projects and tools. Week-by-week structure, what past learners built, and every tool you\'ll touch hands-on. Curriculum 10 · Projects 3 · Tools 12. Curriculum 10 Projects 3 Tools 12 M01IT and networking foundations24 hrs · Wk 1-3", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "How networks really move packetsTCP/IP, DNS, HTTP dissectedLinux command line fluencyWindows administration essentialsLab: build and map a small network"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need to know programming to start in cyber security?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not to start. Networking and Linux matter more for analyst roles. We teach scripting basics where they help, and the lab-first approach means you learn by investigating, not by coding."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is this ethical hacking or defensive security?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Both, deliberately. You learn attacks so you can recognise them, then spend equal depth on SOC, SIEM and incident response, because defensive roles are where most first jobs are."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which certification does the course prepare me for?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "CompTIA Security+ (SY0-701), the baseline global recruiters screen for, with structured mock exams. We also orient you on the CEH pathway. Exams are booked with the bodies and charged separately."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the starting salary in cyber security?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "SOC analysts typically start between Rs 3.5 and 6 lakh. With two years and incident experience, Rs 6 to 11 lakh is common, and specialists climb quickly from there."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is cyber security hard for so