<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>Do I need to know programming to start in cyber security? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Not to start. Networking and Linux matter more for analyst roles. We teach scripting basics where they help, and the lab-first approach means you learn by investigating, not by coding.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is this ethical hacking or defensive security? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both, deliberately. You learn attacks so you can recognise them, then spend equal depth on SOC, SIEM and incident response, because defensive roles are where most first jobs are.</div></details>
<details><summary>Which certification does the course prepare me for? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">CompTIA Security+ (SY0-701), the baseline global recruiters screen for, with structured mock exams. We also orient you on the CEH pathway. Exams are booked with the bodies and charged separately.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the starting salary in cyber security? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">SOC analysts typically start between Rs 3.5 and 6 lakh. With two years and incident experience, Rs 6 to 11 lakh is common, and specialists climb quickly from there.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is cyber security hard for someone from a non-IT background? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">It is demanding but learnable. The first month builds networking and Linux from fundamentals. Curiosity and methodical thinking predict success better than a specific degree.</div></details>
<details><summary>Will I get hands-on lab practice or just theory? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">The course is built around a lab. You attack vulnerable machines, investigate simulated breaches in Splunk and harden cloud accounts. Every module ends in evidence you can show.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala and the GCC. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
